  "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\u03ba(t)=\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and ${T}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}\u20612t+{sin}^{2}\u20612t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}\u20612t+{cos}^{2}\u20612t)+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(t) & =\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
